      "message": "fix(2d): refuse a no-pick chamfer on a partly bevelled edge loop by name\n\nA 2D Chamfer with no picks classified each top loop whole, by the\nfarthest vertex from the wall. A loop with a modelled chamfer on one\nside only read as bevelled (an extra vertex on the bevel's top edge)\nor as sharp (no such vertex). The ride then cut the sharp sides, or\nstood inside the part at the bevel. The verifier refused both as a\ngouge at a coordinate, with no reason.\n\nride_loops now checks each matched top loop per segment (both ends\nand the middle against the wall ring). A loop with a bevelled segment\nand more than one width of sharp length refuses at generation. The\nmessage names the bevelled part and the sharp part and asks for picks.\nThe check does not depend on tessellation.\n\nAll-sharp parts (#303), loops bevelled all round (#2435) and a sharp\nloop beside a bevelled loop (#2596) are unchanged. The verifier is\nunchanged.\n\nFixes #2887\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
